1
00:00:35,791 --> 00:00:36,833
Grandpa!

2
00:00:36,916 --> 00:00:37,750
Pa!

3
00:00:38,625 --> 00:00:39,625
Pa!

4
00:01:39,208 --> 00:01:40,041
Dad.

5
00:01:47,583 --> 00:01:48,416
Pa?

6
00:01:58,166 --> 00:01:59,000
Wat.

7
00:02:00,625 --> 00:02:01,708
Is Aim with you?

8
00:02:09,958 --> 00:02:11,333
We need a flashlight.

9
00:02:11,416 --> 00:02:12,458
I'm looking.

10
00:02:12,541 --> 00:02:13,375
Try up here.

11
00:02:14,583 --> 00:02:16,083
What on earth are you doing?

12
00:02:16,666 --> 00:02:17,750
Dad and Aim are gone.

13
00:02:18,875 --> 00:02:20,125
This doesn't work.

14
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,333
- I think there's another one.
- Keep it down.

15
00:02:23,875 --> 00:02:27,208
Try not to make too much
of a fuss or everyone will show up.

16
00:02:27,291 --> 00:02:29,250
The neighbors, they all hate your dad.

17
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:32,916
They'll call the cops
or they'll wanna perform another exorcism.

18
00:02:33,958 --> 00:02:35,000
Exorcism?

19
00:02:35,083 --> 00:02:37,500
Mom, Dad isn't possessed. He's just sick.

20
00:02:37,583 --> 00:02:39,500
How often is he like this?

21
00:02:39,583 --> 00:02:40,916
Why have you kept this secret?

22
00:02:43,125 --> 00:02:44,750
People around here are mad.

23
00:02:44,833 --> 00:02:48,166
Yeah, well, he's been acting strange
for a while now.

24
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:50,541
But never this bad before.

25
00:02:50,625 --> 00:02:52,250
You two haven't been around to help.

26
00:02:52,333 --> 00:02:53,416
Aim!

27
00:02:54,708 --> 00:02:55,541
Wan.

28
00:03:00,083 --> 00:03:02,250
They can't have gone out the front.
The gate's locked.

29
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:03,166
Yeah.

30
00:03:05,541 --> 00:03:06,416
Aim!

31
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:10,416
Mom, you wait here in case Dad comes back.

32
00:03:11,375 --> 00:03:13,125
And keep your phone on you, okay, Mom?

33
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:15,083
Wan!

34
00:03:21,541 --> 00:03:26,125
<i>Sadhu. </i>May the spirits
of the forest and the mountains

35
00:03:26,208 --> 00:03:27,583
<i>protect them both.</i>

36
00:03:27,666 --> 00:03:29,875
<i>Do not let them be harmed or killed.</i>

37
00:03:29,958 --> 00:03:32,583
<i>Let them return home safely.</i>

38
00:04:44,458 --> 00:04:49,291
DELUSION

39
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:52,750
Pa!

40
00:04:54,125 --> 00:04:55,000
Aim!

41
00:04:57,541 --> 00:04:58,416
Pa!

42
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,500
Wan.

43
00:05:02,166 --> 00:05:03,000
Aim.

44
00:05:09,833 --> 00:05:10,666
Sis.

45
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:12,958
Look at this.

46
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,291
Wan.

47
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,208
Sis.

48
00:05:38,666 --> 00:05:39,500
Aim!

49
00:05:41,458 --> 00:05:42,291
Aim!

50
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:46,333
Wan.

51
00:05:48,041 --> 00:05:48,875
Sis.

52
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,791
Check his phone?

53
00:05:58,791 --> 00:05:59,625
Where is it?

54
00:06:31,125 --> 00:06:33,125
- Aim.
- Grandpa?

55
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:38,458
Grandpa, it hurts. Let go, Grandpa.

56
00:06:38,541 --> 00:06:39,458
You're hurting me.

57
00:06:39,541 --> 00:06:41,125
What the hell are you doing here?

58
00:06:41,208 --> 00:06:42,250
Why did you come here?

59
00:06:43,708 --> 00:06:47,208
How many times have I told you
not to come here anymore?

60
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:50,833
- Let go!
- There are ghosts here.

61
00:06:51,416 --> 00:06:52,708
And they'll make you one, too!

62
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,708
Grandpa, let go.

63
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:56,916
Let go, Grandpa!

64
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:57,875
- Huh?
- Let go.

65
00:06:59,416 --> 00:07:00,750
Please, Grandpa. It hurts.

66
00:07:05,083 --> 00:07:06,458
Grandpa! Let go!

67
00:07:17,791 --> 00:07:18,625
You're okay.

68
00:07:19,666 --> 00:07:20,500
Don't cry.

69
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,583
Don't cry.

70
00:07:25,291 --> 00:07:26,125
Don't cry.

71
00:07:37,583 --> 00:07:39,083
To Big Bird.

72
00:07:39,166 --> 00:07:41,000
Congratulations, sir.

73
00:07:41,083 --> 00:07:42,708
- Good on you, buddy.
- Mmm.

74
00:07:43,791 --> 00:07:46,500
You made superintendent.
What's your secret?

75
00:07:47,041 --> 00:07:48,208
Come on, tell us.

76
00:07:48,291 --> 00:07:49,666
No secret, brother.

77
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,750
I just did my job. That's all.

78
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:53,375
But I promise I won't forget you guys.

79
00:07:54,666 --> 00:07:56,166
Better not, you motherfucker.

80
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:58,208
- I'm behind you, Big Bird.
- Yeah.

81
00:08:10,875 --> 00:08:11,708
Hey.

82
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:13,375
What's the big hurry?

83
00:08:14,833 --> 00:08:15,916
No time to waste,

84
00:08:16,791 --> 00:08:17,833
unlike you guys.

85
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:19,916
You're full of shit.

86
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,666
Your precinct's dead.

87
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:24,375
We both know
it's like a graveyard in there.

88
00:08:28,541 --> 00:08:30,166
Relax the ego, my friend.

89
00:08:30,958 --> 00:08:32,916
Just do whatever the boss tells you to.

90
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,250
You gotta suck up a little bit.

91
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:35,875
That's how you'll get back to Bangkok.

92
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:37,750
Playing the hero

93
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:39,958
won't get you anywhere.

94
00:08:41,166 --> 00:08:42,250
Learn from a master.

95
00:08:47,583 --> 00:08:48,916
I think you're a bit drunk.

96
00:08:49,416 --> 00:08:50,458
Go back and sit down, eh?

97
00:08:52,166 --> 00:08:54,083
Even if you were such a hero,

98
00:08:54,583 --> 00:08:56,041
or some kind of genius,

99
00:08:57,083 --> 00:08:58,750
if your boss doesn't want you…

100
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:03,458
you ain't got nothing.

101
00:09:04,291 --> 00:09:05,125
You get it?

102
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:11,166
Here we go!

103
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:12,583
- Sir Bird.
- Big Bird.

104
00:09:12,666 --> 00:09:14,750
Cheers!

105
00:09:21,750 --> 00:09:24,291
Everybody freeze! Hands up, all of you!

106
00:09:24,375 --> 00:09:25,458
- Don't move.
- Hands up!

107
00:09:25,541 --> 00:09:26,625
Put that down.

108
00:09:26,708 --> 00:09:28,791
- Gather all the evidence.
- Yes, sir.

109
00:09:28,875 --> 00:09:29,708
On the ground.

110
00:09:30,708 --> 00:09:34,375
You're under arrest for operating
an illegal online gambling site,

111
00:09:34,458 --> 00:09:36,625
money laundering, and computer fraud.

112
00:09:36,708 --> 00:09:37,833
Take them away.

113
00:09:37,916 --> 00:09:39,333
- Move!
- Yes, sir.

114
00:09:39,416 --> 00:09:40,875
Come on. Hands up you heads!

115
00:09:43,250 --> 00:09:44,250
On your knees.

116
00:09:56,375 --> 00:09:58,333
So why did you make such a scene?

117
00:09:58,416 --> 00:10:01,791
Your instructions were to keep them
under surveillance and then inform me.

118
00:10:02,708 --> 00:10:05,916
I seized the opportunity to catch them
red handed with the evidence.

119
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,541
And now it's a media circus.

120
00:10:08,666 --> 00:10:10,416
An unauthorized operation.

121
00:10:13,291 --> 00:10:15,625
If you have a problem
with the way I do things around here,

122
00:10:16,708 --> 00:10:18,541
you could be better working
somewhere else.

123
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:28,000
I apologize
for my officer's behavior, sir.

124
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:30,416
We're gonna need about ten million
to put this to bed…

125
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:48,083
Hello?

126
00:10:50,541 --> 00:10:51,750
How long will you be?

127
00:10:53,583 --> 00:10:55,416
Okay. Thanks. See you soon.

128
00:10:58,750 --> 00:10:59,750
I think we're close.

129
00:11:09,958 --> 00:11:10,833
You hear that?

130
00:11:27,875 --> 00:11:28,708
Aim!

131
00:11:32,666 --> 00:11:34,375
Aim, can you hear me?

132
00:11:34,458 --> 00:11:35,416
Aim.

133
00:11:38,791 --> 00:11:42,416
Sis, wait. What are you doing?
Where are you going? Sis.

134
00:11:43,416 --> 00:11:44,458
Calm down, sis.

135
00:11:46,875 --> 00:11:48,166
I'm here. Don't worry.

136
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:50,875
Take a deep breath.

137
00:11:50,958 --> 00:11:52,416
That's it. Breathe slowly.

138
00:12:00,666 --> 00:12:01,500
Wan.

139
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:04,000
I think if we go in there now

140
00:12:04,833 --> 00:12:06,583
where there's no trail to follow,

141
00:12:07,250 --> 00:12:09,125
we could get hopelessly lost.

142
00:12:09,666 --> 00:12:11,250
And then we will never find them.

143
00:12:13,458 --> 00:12:15,000
Wat, we can't see if he's looking.

144
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:20,125
We should head back to base and wait.

145
00:12:20,208 --> 00:12:21,833
Wait for help to arrive.

146
00:12:23,166 --> 00:12:24,666
If you end up missing too,

147
00:12:25,375 --> 00:12:26,750
things will just be worse.

148
00:12:29,458 --> 00:12:30,791
Let's go back and wait.

149
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:34,125
Come on, sis. Let's go.

150
00:12:58,541 --> 00:12:59,375
Hello, ma'am.

151
00:12:59,958 --> 00:13:00,916
Where's your daughter?

152
00:13:02,625 --> 00:13:03,958
What's the old man up to?

153
00:13:06,375 --> 00:13:08,208
He'll be back in a little while.

154
00:13:08,291 --> 00:13:10,125
He went out for a walk.

155
00:13:10,208 --> 00:13:11,625
The kids, they're out looking.

156
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:13,958
He took your grandchild with him.

157
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:16,500
When did they go missing?

158
00:13:16,583 --> 00:13:18,083
I don't know what time it was.

159
00:13:19,666 --> 00:13:21,041
Anyway, you're the police.

160
00:13:21,125 --> 00:13:23,791
So why are you standing
around here asking questions?

161
00:13:23,875 --> 00:13:26,708
You're not from around here.
How could you help anyway?

162
00:13:39,958 --> 00:13:42,916
Officer, I found Aim's tablet
in the forest.

163
00:14:10,125 --> 00:14:11,416
It's coming on now.

164
00:14:38,458 --> 00:14:42,000
Does dementia normally cause
noses to bleed like that, doctor?

165
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,208
Uh, no.

166
00:14:51,125 --> 00:14:52,625
So that means it's not normal.

167
00:14:57,500 --> 00:15:00,166
Even if he's not acting so rational,

168
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:02,083
my dad would hurt his own grandson.

169
00:15:11,625 --> 00:15:13,000
Why did you call the police?

170
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:16,583
It's just add to people
calling him possessed.

171
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:18,666
As if we don't have
enough to do right now.

172
00:15:19,458 --> 00:15:20,833
That's all you care about?

173
00:15:22,041 --> 00:15:23,291
What about your grandson?

174
00:15:23,375 --> 00:15:25,083
Of course I care.

175
00:15:25,166 --> 00:15:27,833
This is a family matter.
We should handle it.

176
00:15:27,916 --> 00:15:29,791
What are we going to do now?

177
00:15:29,875 --> 00:15:33,375
If the police arrest him and lock him up,
what will we do then?

178
00:15:40,083 --> 00:15:41,583
Can you tell me what Aim was wearing?

179
00:15:42,833 --> 00:15:46,291
A T-shirt, light green,
and plaid pajama pants.

180
00:15:47,166 --> 00:15:48,083
Okay.

181
00:15:48,166 --> 00:15:50,625
I'm gonna head out now.
You just wait out here.

182
00:15:50,708 --> 00:15:52,416
A patrol unit will be here soon.

183
00:15:55,583 --> 00:15:56,583
This is Sasidit.

184
00:15:56,666 --> 00:15:59,500
The child is 150 centimeters tall.

185
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:02,375
He's wearing a light green T-shirt
and plaid pajama pants.

186
00:16:03,041 --> 00:16:05,333
Sergent, when you arrive,
check around the house first,

187
00:16:05,416 --> 00:16:06,500
and split up into teams.

188
00:16:07,875 --> 00:16:09,041
<i>Copy that.</i>

189
00:16:10,458 --> 00:16:11,666
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

190
00:16:20,208 --> 00:16:23,125
I grew up here. I won't be a burden.

191
00:16:27,916 --> 00:16:30,041
Wat, don't go with them.

192
00:16:30,125 --> 00:16:32,250
Stay with me here. I'm scared.

193
00:16:35,041 --> 00:16:36,083
Be careful, sis.

194
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:41,250
Hey.

195
00:17:00,291 --> 00:17:02,625
Let's go home, Grandpa.

196
00:17:02,708 --> 00:17:04,750
Listen, why are you crying for? Eh?

197
00:17:26,583 --> 00:17:27,875
Here, you take this.

198
00:17:29,791 --> 00:17:32,416
You said you wanted to go fishing
at the waterfall.

199
00:17:33,708 --> 00:17:35,000
That's where I'm taking you.

200
00:17:36,541 --> 00:17:37,625
So don't cry.

201
00:17:38,916 --> 00:17:40,250
You're the one who wanted it.

202
00:18:08,458 --> 00:18:10,416
Nothing to report here as of yet.

203
00:18:11,125 --> 00:18:13,166
<i>Waterfall.</i>

204
00:18:13,250 --> 00:18:14,625
<i>I'll go there and check it out</i>

205
00:18:15,583 --> 00:18:18,208
Sergeant, I missed that. Say it again.

206
00:18:18,291 --> 00:18:20,458
He said something about the waterfall.

207
00:18:20,541 --> 00:18:21,875
It's not too far from here.

208
00:18:24,625 --> 00:18:26,458
Okay, Sergeant. Check it out.

209
00:18:26,541 --> 00:18:28,291
- Keep me updated, okay?
<i>- Yes, sir.</i>

210
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:30,333
Aim.

211
00:18:31,916 --> 00:18:32,750
Aim.

212
00:18:35,291 --> 00:18:37,083
I think your dad is deteriorating.

213
00:18:37,875 --> 00:18:38,833
How would you know?

214
00:18:40,125 --> 00:18:40,958
He…

215
00:18:42,041 --> 00:18:43,500
These episodes, they're…

216
00:18:44,333 --> 00:18:45,791
happening more often now.

217
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,750
He may present a danger to others.

218
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:50,416
So what should I do?

219
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:53,958
I don't know, I guess
you just have to work it out, that's all.

220
00:18:54,041 --> 00:18:57,208
It's a family matters,
but if this keeps happening,

221
00:18:57,291 --> 00:18:58,875
then things will only get worse.

222
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,500
And now he's lost in a forest
with a child.

223
00:19:02,583 --> 00:19:03,750
What on earth is he thinking?

224
00:19:04,708 --> 00:19:06,958
Once he gets his medication,
he'll be fine.

225
00:19:10,291 --> 00:19:12,708
My dad's not violent.
He won't hurt anyone.

226
00:19:15,166 --> 00:19:16,166
Aim!

227
00:19:20,166 --> 00:19:21,166
Aim!

228
00:19:30,541 --> 00:19:32,000
Here, Mom. Let me help.

229
00:19:32,083 --> 00:19:33,083
I'm okay.

230
00:19:34,583 --> 00:19:37,083
Your sister, she's never much helps to me.

231
00:19:37,166 --> 00:19:40,583
Who knows what she does over
at her rich husband's house?

232
00:19:40,666 --> 00:19:43,416
They're probably thinking
her parents didn't raise her properly.

233
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:45,250
Here, eat up.

234
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:05,041
Mom, aren't you scared about Dad?

235
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:16,708
If he died or just vanished,
that's still better than possessed.

236
00:20:28,250 --> 00:20:29,250
Nee.

237
00:20:32,208 --> 00:20:33,208
Hello, Uncle.

238
00:20:35,208 --> 00:20:38,083
It's been a while, hasn't it?
Have you been well?

239
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:48,083
Mom, your brother's here.

240
00:21:03,041 --> 00:21:05,750
Phii Pong, he hasn't
brought the boy back yet?

241
00:21:12,666 --> 00:21:13,500
Here.

242
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,291
Write Aim's name here on the chest.

243
00:21:18,416 --> 00:21:20,375
And if Narong comes back,

244
00:21:20,458 --> 00:21:22,708
I'll perform a quick ritual.

245
00:21:22,791 --> 00:21:24,375
It will help him a lot.

246
00:21:30,708 --> 00:21:33,458
Uh, uncle, you need to stop
all these nonsense.

247
00:21:33,541 --> 00:21:35,000
My father is just ill.

248
00:21:36,916 --> 00:21:37,916
And what's this?

249
00:21:38,958 --> 00:21:40,583
Please just take it away.

250
00:21:40,666 --> 00:21:43,333
No, you keep it.

251
00:21:44,041 --> 00:21:46,458
The ghost will not leave easily.

252
00:21:46,541 --> 00:21:49,375
It must be exorcised or it will never go.

253
00:21:49,458 --> 00:21:52,625
A boy from the city like you
doesn't know these things.

254
00:21:53,125 --> 00:21:56,416
Your mother, she grew up with this forest.

255
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:59,083
She knows what needs to be done.

256
00:22:01,791 --> 00:22:04,208
Uh, okay then, Uncle. You know what?

257
00:22:05,333 --> 00:22:06,875
Let's just go our own ways.

258
00:22:07,458 --> 00:22:09,958
I'll see to it that Dad
gets medical treatment

259
00:22:10,041 --> 00:22:12,708
and you go ahead
and do whatever rituals you like.

260
00:22:14,125 --> 00:22:17,208
But I want you
to leave my parents out of it.

261
00:22:18,125 --> 00:22:19,125
Promise me that.

262
00:22:22,791 --> 00:22:26,625
The modern medicines,
they can't cure things like these.

263
00:22:27,541 --> 00:22:32,208
A shaman like me, I've saved
more lives than you could count.

264
00:22:32,916 --> 00:22:35,208
Let me know what you decide, sister.

265
00:23:03,041 --> 00:23:04,041
Aim!

266
00:23:04,875 --> 00:23:05,875
Aim!

267
00:23:06,666 --> 00:23:07,666
Aim!

268
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:08,750
Aim!

269
00:23:12,958 --> 00:23:14,500
- Aim!
- Aim!

270
00:23:16,375 --> 00:23:17,333
Aim.

271
00:23:29,916 --> 00:23:31,250
Aim!

272
00:23:33,708 --> 00:23:35,458
Hey. Step back. Step back.

273
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:38,875
This is a crime scene.

274
00:23:38,958 --> 00:23:41,083
You must listen.
Just wait here and let me see.

275
00:24:05,875 --> 00:24:06,875
Sergeant, you copy?

276
00:24:06,958 --> 00:24:08,416
I found a body.

277
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:10,625
It looks like Mued, the first missing boy.

278
00:24:11,625 --> 00:24:13,083
I'm not far from the waterfall.

279
00:24:14,125 --> 00:24:16,666
Look for a large tree
wrapped in three-colored ribbons.

280
00:24:17,666 --> 00:24:20,541
Notify the station
and get the medical examiner down here.

281
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:21,541
Over.

282
00:24:23,625 --> 00:24:24,625
Aim's…

283
00:24:29,833 --> 00:24:30,833
Come in, Sergeant.

284
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:33,375
I believe Aim is not far from my location.

285
00:24:38,500 --> 00:24:39,875
Grandpa.

286
00:24:42,541 --> 00:24:44,125
Grandpa.

287
00:24:55,916 --> 00:24:56,750
Hurry up.

288
00:24:56,833 --> 00:25:00,958
Grandpa, we should go home.
Mom will be worried.

289
00:25:07,750 --> 00:25:09,666
Look, can you see the fish?

290
00:25:10,625 --> 00:25:11,708
You wanna see?

291
00:25:12,583 --> 00:25:13,625
Go on. Look.

292
00:25:16,250 --> 00:25:18,833
Over there, see, so many fish. Look.

293
00:25:20,333 --> 00:25:24,208
Can you see? Look, there.
See, there are fish.

294
00:25:24,291 --> 00:25:25,750
Right here, and over there.

295
00:25:26,916 --> 00:25:27,833
Fish.

296
00:25:29,166 --> 00:25:32,166
The fish, there, right here. Lots of them.

297
00:25:32,875 --> 00:25:34,250
So many fish.

298
00:25:35,166 --> 00:25:36,375
Right here, look.

299
00:25:46,541 --> 00:25:47,541
Where are you going?

300
00:25:49,375 --> 00:25:50,666
Don't you want to see the fish?

301
00:25:52,791 --> 00:25:54,916
Grandpa, I'm scared.

302
00:26:09,166 --> 00:26:10,791
I am not your grandpa.

303
00:26:13,291 --> 00:26:16,125
Kids like you are no good.

304
00:26:17,250 --> 00:26:20,458
You need to learn. I'm going to teach you.

305
00:26:21,166 --> 00:26:22,000
Phii Pong.

306
00:26:22,083 --> 00:26:23,750
You really are Phii Pong.

307
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:26,875
Help, Mom!

308
00:26:26,958 --> 00:26:28,125
Help!

309
00:26:28,208 --> 00:26:29,208
Mom!

310
00:26:39,708 --> 00:26:41,416
Naughty kids like you…

311
00:26:42,500 --> 00:26:44,500
belong here in the forest.

312
00:26:44,583 --> 00:26:46,458
You're not going home to your mom.

313
00:26:46,541 --> 00:26:48,541
Go on. Get in the water.

314
00:26:48,625 --> 00:26:49,625
Now!

315
00:26:53,541 --> 00:26:55,500
No, don't, Grandpa. Don't!

316
00:26:56,541 --> 00:26:58,791
I don't want to. Grandpa, let go.

317
00:26:58,875 --> 00:27:00,875
Grandpa, don't!

318
00:27:00,958 --> 00:27:02,833
Grandpa!

319
00:27:02,916 --> 00:27:03,916
Let go, Grandpa.

320
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,708
Grandpa, I want to go home.

321
00:27:07,791 --> 00:27:08,708
Let me go!

322
00:27:09,708 --> 00:27:10,916
Get into the water.

323
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:13,125
- No, Grandpa! No!
- Go!

324
00:27:13,208 --> 00:27:14,541
Let me go!

325
00:28:05,375 --> 00:28:06,791
Aim! Aim!

326
00:28:19,583 --> 00:28:20,583
Aim!

327
00:28:22,291 --> 00:28:23,291
Calm down.

328
00:28:25,750 --> 00:28:26,750
I've got you.

329
00:28:26,833 --> 00:28:27,833
You're safe now.

330
00:28:39,208 --> 00:28:40,208
Aim.

331
00:28:40,791 --> 00:28:42,125
Aim.

332
00:28:42,208 --> 00:28:43,541
Aim.

333
00:28:43,625 --> 00:28:44,666
Aim.

334
00:28:45,916 --> 00:28:46,750
Aim.

335
00:28:53,666 --> 00:28:54,708
Aim.

336
00:28:54,791 --> 00:28:55,625
Aim.

337
00:28:59,541 --> 00:29:01,500
Aim.

338
00:29:02,125 --> 00:29:03,125
Aim.

339
00:29:06,125 --> 00:29:07,208
Aim.

340
00:29:07,291 --> 00:29:08,125
Aim, son.

341
00:29:08,208 --> 00:29:09,208
Over there.

342
00:29:13,041 --> 00:29:14,166
Take him away.

343
00:29:14,708 --> 00:29:15,541
Come on.

344
00:29:17,291 --> 00:29:18,125
Aim.

345
00:29:19,541 --> 00:29:20,541
Come on now.

346
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,000
Let's go.

347
00:30:29,041 --> 00:30:30,083
Have you got a bandage?

348
00:30:33,291 --> 00:30:34,208
Inspector.

349
00:30:37,666 --> 00:30:40,250
Could you please tell the other officers

350
00:30:41,166 --> 00:30:42,583
to be gentle with my father?

351
00:30:44,041 --> 00:30:45,041
He's quite confused.

352
00:31:07,583 --> 00:31:08,416
Aim.

353
00:31:12,375 --> 00:31:13,458
You see what you've done?

354
00:31:14,708 --> 00:31:17,291
All you do is bringing trouble
to our house.

355
00:32:07,083 --> 00:32:09,416
We did everything Sak told us to.

356
00:32:10,625 --> 00:32:12,750
But my grandson still isn't here.

357
00:32:15,833 --> 00:32:18,625
Please calm down, and don't cry.

358
00:32:19,708 --> 00:32:21,291
Wait for the shaman to speak.

359
00:32:23,791 --> 00:32:25,750
It's all right.

360
00:32:26,833 --> 00:32:27,833
Let her cry.

361
00:32:35,125 --> 00:32:36,833
Her grandson is already dead.

362
00:32:38,208 --> 00:32:40,208
See, the ghost has taken him.

363
00:32:41,583 --> 00:32:44,500
It is an evil force.
There's nothing more to do.

364
00:32:59,458 --> 00:33:02,000
Collect the soil and the teeth,
have them all tested.

365
00:33:03,083 --> 00:33:04,916
The killer must've left something behind.

366
00:33:06,833 --> 00:33:08,958
But what kind of evidence
would a ghost leave?

367
00:33:10,208 --> 00:33:11,875
You must be careful, Inspector.

368
00:33:12,791 --> 00:33:14,625
The ghost could possess any of us.

369
00:33:16,416 --> 00:33:18,291
If the killer really is a ghost,

370
00:33:18,375 --> 00:33:20,166
then we shall arrest that ghost.

371
00:33:28,083 --> 00:33:29,750
You shouldn't joke, Inspector.

372
00:33:30,916 --> 00:33:34,458
You know, locals believe
in this Phii Pong.

373
00:33:36,458 --> 00:33:40,708
And decades ago, right here
at the same spot, a child was killed.

374
00:33:41,625 --> 00:33:42,750
Lying face down.

375
00:33:44,291 --> 00:33:45,291
Like this.

376
00:33:47,125 --> 00:33:49,458
Teeth and guts ripped out, just the same.

377
00:33:52,250 --> 00:33:53,583
Sergeant.

378
00:33:53,666 --> 00:33:54,666
I think the people here…

379
00:33:55,791 --> 00:33:57,416
have seen too many horror movies.

380
00:33:58,541 --> 00:34:00,583
How does a spirit pick up a knife?

381
00:34:00,666 --> 00:34:02,875
And then rips someone's guts out, eh?

382
00:34:12,875 --> 00:34:14,000
Please forgive me.

383
00:34:29,333 --> 00:34:31,041
It's about your grandson, ma'am.

384
00:34:31,125 --> 00:34:33,208
I'm sorry to tell you,

385
00:34:33,291 --> 00:34:36,166
police have located
his body in the forest.

386
00:34:36,958 --> 00:34:38,041
Right now, the body is…

387
00:34:38,125 --> 00:34:39,791
Tell us what to do.

388
00:34:39,875 --> 00:34:41,416
Please guide us, shaman.

389
00:34:43,541 --> 00:34:46,208
We must first find out

390
00:34:46,291 --> 00:34:47,833
who it inhabits.

391
00:34:49,791 --> 00:34:50,791
Anyone…

392
00:34:51,416 --> 00:34:55,166
who has been lurking
around the forest during these nights,

393
00:34:55,250 --> 00:35:00,083
someone acting strangely
with darkness to their face

394
00:35:00,166 --> 00:35:04,291
from this twisted being, we must exorcise

395
00:35:04,375 --> 00:35:06,500
the ghost within.

396
00:35:18,250 --> 00:35:19,541
We found hairs on the body.

397
00:35:20,541 --> 00:35:23,666
The DNA test maybe able
to identify our suspect.

398
00:35:28,625 --> 00:35:30,583
You don't remember anything?

399
00:35:31,416 --> 00:35:32,666
You understand what I'm saying?

400
00:35:42,250 --> 00:35:43,083
A little help.

401
00:35:44,875 --> 00:35:45,708
Hey.

402
00:36:08,208 --> 00:36:09,458
<i>How's Aim doing?</i>

403
00:36:10,541 --> 00:36:12,083
He's under observation.

404
00:36:12,916 --> 00:36:14,958
But I think he'll be okay.

405
00:36:16,375 --> 00:36:18,291
That's such a relief to hear.

406
00:36:18,375 --> 00:36:19,375
Mmm.

407
00:36:21,375 --> 00:36:22,666
How's Dad getting along?

408
00:36:26,875 --> 00:36:27,833
Sis, I have to go.

409
00:36:28,416 --> 00:36:29,666
How is he, Officer?

410
00:36:30,833 --> 00:36:32,416
Can you tell us how my is father?

411
00:36:32,500 --> 00:36:34,125
He hasn't responded to anything.

412
00:36:35,250 --> 00:36:38,333
But, Shaman, won't this
make things worse for Aunt Nee?

413
00:36:39,416 --> 00:36:40,791
I warned her.

414
00:36:41,458 --> 00:36:44,833
I told her to exorcise Phii Pong.

415
00:36:46,208 --> 00:36:48,083
And now someone's dead.

416
00:36:50,208 --> 00:36:52,041
<i>My grandson is fine now.</i>

417
00:36:52,125 --> 00:36:54,666
And his mother won't to press any charges.

418
00:36:54,750 --> 00:36:56,166
Can you let him go?

419
00:36:56,250 --> 00:36:57,708
This is a murder case.

420
00:36:57,791 --> 00:36:59,416
He's now a suspect.

421
00:36:59,500 --> 00:37:01,875
I'm sorry, ma'am,
we're unable to release him.

422
00:42:55,583 --> 00:43:00,583
Subtitle translation by: Parida Kim
